From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: wait up to two beacon intervals for the frames of a
 removed link

After the removal TBTT, hostapd waits a quarter of a beacon interval for
the TX status of the Disassociation and Deauthentication frames before
it stops the link. The driver holds such a frame for a STA in power save
or off the channel until the STA is back, which is often after the next
Beacon frame, and the stop of the link drops it. A STA then learns of
the removal only by its link loss.

IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 35.3.6.3 has the frame sent before the BSS
terminates and lets the BSS terminate after the TBTT. Wait up to two
beacon intervals. The TX status of the last frame still ends the wait,
so the link stops as before where every STA is awake. removal_ms grows
by the same amount and stays the latest time the link stops.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -537,9 +537,12 @@ static void hostapd_link_remove_timeout_register(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 }
 
 
+/* The driver holds the frame to a STA in power save or off the channel until
+ * the STA is back, which is often after the next Beacon frame, and the end of
+ * the BSS drops it */
 static unsigned int hostapd_link_remove_tx_wait_us(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 {
-	return TU_TO_USEC(hapd->iconf->beacon_int) / 4;
+	return 2 * TU_TO_USEC(hapd->iconf->beacon_int);
 }
 
 
